          "statement": "1. Let $G = (V_1 \\cup V_2, E)$ be a bipartite graph. Prove that if $G$ is Hamiltonian, then $|V_1| = |V_2|$. Deduce that any bipartite graph on an odd number of vertices cannot be Hamiltonian. 2. In a 3-dimensional cube graph $Q_3$, determine whether $Q_3$ is Eulerian, semi-Eulerian, or Hamiltonian.",
