          "statement": "1. Consider a tree $T$ with 9 vertices labeled $1, \\dots, 9$ and edge set $E = \\{\\{1, 2\\}, \\{2, 3\\}, \\{3, 4\\}, \\{4, 5\\}, \\{3, 6\\}, \\{6, 7\\}, \\{7, 8\\}, \\{7, 9\\}\\}$. Determine the eccentricity of every vertex, the radius $\\text{rad}(T)$, the diameter $\\text{diam}(T)$, and all center vertices $Z(T)$. 2. Execute Kruskal's algorithm on a 5-vertex network with edges: $\\{A, B\\}: 1$, $\\{B, C\\}: 4$, $\\{A, C\\}: 3$, $\\{C, D\\}: 2$, $\\{D, E\\}: 5$, $\\{C, E\\}: 6$, $\\{B, D\\}: 7$. List the edges added in order and state the total MST weight.",
