          "statement": "1. Given the Prüfer sequence $P = (3, 3, 4, 1, 4)$, reconstruct the unique labeled tree on 7 vertices. 2. Encode the tree with edges $\\{\\{1, 4\\}, \\{2, 4\\}, \\{3, 4\\}, \\{4, 5\\}, \\{5, 6\\}\\}$ into its Prüfer sequence. 3. Prove that in every tree on $n \\ge 2$ vertices, there are at least two leaves (vertices of degree 1).",
