          "title": "Complete Formal Proof of Landau's Theorem on Tournament Scores",
          "question": "Provide a complete, mathematically rigorous proof of Landau's Theorem (Theorem 6.5): A non-decreasing sequence of non-negative integers $s_1 \\le s_2 \\le \\dots \\le s_n$ is the score sequence of a tournament on $n$ vertices if and only if $\\sum_{i=1}^k s_i \\ge \\binom{k}{2}$ for all $1 \\le k \\le n - 1$, and $\\sum_{i=1}^n s_i = \\binom{n}{2}$.",
          "statement": "Provide a complete, mathematically rigorous proof of Landau's Theorem (Theorem 6.5): A non-decreasing sequence of non-negative integers $s_1 \\le s_2 \\le \\dots \\le s_n$ is the score sequence of a tournament on $n$ vertices if and only if $\\sum_{i=1}^k s_i \\ge \\binom{k}{2}$ for all $1 \\le k \\le n - 1$, and $\\sum_{i=1}^n s_i = \\binom{n}{2}$.",
