          "title": "Euler's Formula on Platonic Solids & Maximal Planar Faces",
          "question": "1. Verify Euler's formula $V - E + F = 2$ for the 1-skeletons of all five Platonic solids: (a) Regular Tetrahedron, (b) Cube (Hexahedron), (c) Regular Octahedron, (d) Regular Dodecahedron, (e) Regular Icosahedron. 2. A connected planar graph has 10 vertices and 15 edges. Determine the exact number of faces in any planar embedding of $G$.",
          "statement": "1. Verify Euler's formula $V - E + F = 2$ for the 1-skeletons of all five Platonic solids: (a) Regular Tetrahedron, (b) Cube (Hexahedron), (c) Regular Octahedron, (d) Regular Dodecahedron, (e) Regular Icosahedron. 2. A connected planar graph has 10 vertices and 15 edges. Determine the exact number of faces in any planar embedding of $G$.",
